 "blockers": [
  {
   "where": "T4 V4 row (L272), MSA-7 cut reason order (L174, L1611), MSA-21 (L282), AC-MSA-151 (L1708)",
   "issue": "The ADR-0015 sync added to V4 (`can_rebase_detach`) that it \"also returns `BDY_REBASE_ACTOR_IN_CAP`\", but nothing downstream was reconciled. V4 runs before V5 and before `CUT_BLOCKED` in the MSA-7 reason order, and the order list (L174, L1611) still names only UNKNOWN_BODY, POSE_OUT_OF_RANGE and VEL_OUT_OF_RANGE for V4. So a cut with an actor in the hatch now has two competing outcomes: V4 rejects with `body.BDY_REBASE_ACTOR_IN_CAP` for every origin, or V5 gives `MSA.CUT_BLOCKED` (CHANNEL) / defers (CASCADE, MSA-22). MSA-21 still says V5 is the only safety on both paths, that BM4's net is never reached in a clean build, and that V4 and the reason order are unchanged. ADR-0015 section 9 says the V4 check makes a PLAYER cut refused and a SYSTEM cut deferred, which collides with the CASCADE-defers rule unless the GDD says how the two map. AC-MSA-151 (V5 bypassed by a test hook, A4 receives the error from BM4) is no longer reachable as written: V4 now rejects it before A3, so the test never reaches A4 unless V4 is bypassed too.",
   "fix": "State one ruling in MSA-21 and the T4 V4/V5 rows. Either (a) V4's ACTOR_IN_CAP is the same check as V5's: keep CUT_BLOCKED / defer as the player-facing and cascade outcome, map or suppress the Body reason, and say V4's ACTOR_IN_CAP is unreachable once V5 passes; or (b) add ACTOR_IN_CAP to the MSA-7 order and say how CHANNEL and CASCADE treat it. Then correct MSA-21's \"V4 and the reason order are unchanged\", add the reason to L174 and L1611, and change AC-MSA-151 to bypass both V4 and V5 (or add a V4 AC for the new reason). Tag with *(Amended 2026-10-29 — ADR-0015 sync)*."
  }
 ]
